@Jon 
I got MII, and the first video game I played was Pong. In a pizza parlor. As a teenager. Haven't played many since then, either. In other words, I am completely and totally not a gamer. But when I discovered MII in an earlier puzzle, I thought, oooh I'm gonna try to remember that. Much like learning WII earlier. I didn't get MII right away, but I did eventually. Yay! Helps that it's sort of punny. 

Anyway, yeah, that was a tough cross, but doable for me, a non-gamer.

@Mean Old Lady

I’ve never played on a WII—I remembered MII from an earlier puzzle—and I guess the “customizable” was a subtle hint to the “MII” part of it if you haven’t heard of it. If you get T_CHA I suppose an I is  the most likely guess although TACHA is not impossible and maybe MAI could be a thing (pronounced MY) so maybe that is a bit of a Natick. For me like others it was ART/ACT so I had to get rid of that. On top of that I BoosterTEAMS (groups of parents or alumni who raise money for their kids’ sports? Seems possible to me?) so if I hadn’t heard of HAROLDRAMIS and thought RAMIT could be his last name I would have been completely at sea. So it’s fair to say this was a Naticky corner but I don’t think any of the references were really off limits (she’s in the hall of fame after all, and if I choose not follow the WNBA that’s on me) and if I had failed I still would have liked this puzzle and been happy to learn some new things.

You’ve still got some cruciverbal chops on you, MOL, don’t kick yourself to the curb just yet.

