@HeathieJ @Lynn
 Can we start a whole new thread/rant about buying shoes and the awful uncomfortableness of many women's shoes?I was pretty solid on the 'P' so never thought of INSOLES but INSTEPS isn't what I think of on the much-dreaded occasions where I need new shoes.
  What matters first is where the arch falls..is that INSTEP? After that width but also if the heel will be loose.
  My leading peeve is that companies don't stay consistent! Once I finally find a near-perfect one, they stop making it.

@RozzieGrandma
Yep. You can generally replace the insole, but not the instep. I have a few favorite brands. My big thing is I want a large enough toe box that I can wiggle my toes. No squishy pointy shapes.

So--hiking boots and good leather walking shoes. Fortunately a lot of people in my profession seem to agree.

